</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hansen</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><source>Helminth Diseases of Small Ruminants in the Tropics: A Review of Epidemiology and Control Strategies.: 22-25 April 1996; Bogor, Indonesia.					</source><year>1996</year><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>127</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tinar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Akyol</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name><name><surname>Cirak</surname><given-names>VY</given-names></name><name><surname>Senlik</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Investigations on the seasonal patterns of strongyle infections in grazing lambs, and the occurrence of anthelmintic resistance on sheep and goat farms in western Anatolia, Turkey</article-title><source>Parasitol Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15765247</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00436-005-1312-z</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Wyk</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bath</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The FAMACHA system for managing haemonchosis in sheep and goats by clinically identifying individual animals for treatment</article-title><source>Vet Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>509</fpage><lpage>529</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12387487</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1051/vetres:2002036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waller</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Management and control of nematode parasites of small ruminants in the face of total anthelmintic failure</article-title><source>Trop Biomed</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16493393</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Polley</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bickis</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gastrointestinal nematode parasites in Saskatchewan cattle: egg count distributions in beef animals</article-title><source>Can J Vet Res</source><year>1987</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>469</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3453265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Agyei</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seasonal changes in the level of infective strongylate nematode larvae on pasture in the coastal savanna regions of Ghana</article-title><source>Vet Parasitol</source><year>1997</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>175</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9195721</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-4017(96)01101-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horak</surname><given-names>IG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The seasonal incidence of the major nematode genera recovered from sheep, cattle, impala and blesbok in the Transvaal</article-title><source>J S Afr Vet Assoc</source><year>1981</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7198149</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grant</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></